          "nudge_reason": null,
          "final_text_tail": "Only the intended file is modified. The task is complete.\n\nI added the `get_image_mimetype()` method to `ImageBlock` in `llama-index-core/llama_index/core/base/llms/types.py`:\n\n- **Lazy resolution**: returns the cached `image_mimetype` if already set; otherwise guesses it via `filetype.guess` (from `self.image` bytes, or by resolving `path`/`url` through `resolve_image`).\n- **Caching**: stores the result in `self.image_mimetype` so subsequent calls are O(1).\n- **Decoupling**: `image_to_base64` now delegates to `get_image_mimetype()` instead of inlining the guess logic, so MIME resolution is reusable by any component.\n- Preserves user-provided mimetypes and returns `None` when no source is present.\n\nAll 12 existing tests in `test_types.py` pass, and syntax validates.\n\nNote: I verified against the local repo file directly (the venv's site-packages has a separate installed copy of `llama_index`, so I forced the local `llama-index-core` onto `sys.path` to confirm the change takes effect there).",
